  "term": "felbamate",
  "definition": "Felbamate is a drug with anticonvulsant and antiepileptic effects that reduces seizure activity by dampening excitatory signaling in the brain. Its exact action is not fully known, but it may block NMDA-related glycine activity and weakly affect GABA receptor binding.",
